# AGENTS.md

## New Minecraft Mod Project Protocol

- Before starting any new Minecraft mod project, read `~/.config/opencode/PROJECT_PLANNING.md`
- Ask all clarifying questions from the checklist before writing code
- Propose complete architecture and wait for confirmation before implementing
- If making 3+ commits that change the same core mechanism (trigger, area, timing), pause and ask for detailed requirements

## Browser Launching

- When the user asks to open a browser, immediately launch a new, separate Chrome instance. Do not inspect, attach to, kill, or otherwise manage Chrome instances launched by other sessions, and never kill or restart the user's main Chrome.
- Do not report on or worry about other sessions' browsers unless the user asks about them.
- Working recipe (macOS):
  `open -na "Google Chrome" --args --remote-debugging-port=9222 --remote-allow-origins='*' --user-data-dir="<fresh temp dir>/chrome-profile" --no-first-run --no-default-browser-check "<URL>"`
  Then connect with the `chrome-devtools-existing` tools (they attach to port 9222) and use those for all further browsing/automation in the session.
- A fresh `user-data-dir` means no saved logins — warn the user they will need to log in manually to any sites.
- If port 9222 is already in use by an instance launched earlier in this same session, reuse that instance via the `chrome-devtools-existing` tools instead of launching another.

## Instruction Feedback

- When a user instruction is clear enough to execute but is materially ambiguous, under-specified, or likely to cause the wrong implementation, provide brief feedback on how the instruction could be written more precisely.
- Give this feedback after completing the requested task unless the ambiguity blocks progress.
- Keep the feedback concise: explain the ambiguity and provide one improved example phrasing.
- Do not give instruction-writing feedback for minor wording issues that do not affect implementation.
